\PYG{l+s+s2}{    \PYGZbs{}n4. Count how many of these 12 anthropomorphic figures have at least one visible hand}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    (fingers or hand structure visible, not tucked inside sleeves or purely animal paws/hooves).}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    \PYGZbs{}n5. Provide the final count as the answer.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}
\PYG{+w}{    }\PYG{n+nt}{\PYGZdq{}context\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{:}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The year 2015 was the Year of the Ram/Goat.}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    The exhibition at the Met was likely titled \PYGZsq{}Celebrating the Year of the Ram\PYGZsq{}.}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    There is a famous set of 12 zodiac figures in their collection.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}
